/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/combo_exec_5545f144_20260506_103258/review_4_attempt_1.log:395:    # Arrow-like triangle (4 pixels: tip + stem + two base corners)
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/combo_exec_5545f144_20260506_103258/review_4_attempt_1.log:622:    - Each frame contains one actor-colored triangle plus marker-colored mini-arrow glyphs whose center cells are future landing points.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/combo_exec_5545f144_20260506_103258/review_4_attempt_1.log:627:    - When a marker is consumed, the marker's own arrow sets the new facing; if markers remain, that arrow direction must also be the direction of the next marker that will be consumed from the new head.
/home/lixinyu/snap/new/tmp/combo_exec_5545f144_20260506_103258/review_4_attempt_1.log:630:    Key insight: The triangle tip tells you which marker is eaten now, while the eaten marker's arrow tells you how the sprite must face for the next leg, so every step couples local consumption with one-step lookahead.
